WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 6.8 · MEAL: Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability & Learning
Evaluation

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Evaluation asks whether your work achieves its outcomes and why: is it needed, and does it work?

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:27.022
Evaluation asks deeper questions than monitoring: did the work achieve its outcomes, for whom, why, at what cost and with what unintended effects? For something new: is it needed, and does it work?

4
00:00:27.422 --> 00:00:28.022
Types for different purposes

5
00:00:28.022 --> 00:00:36.389
Formative: Improves the work during delivery; it suits a pilot. For example: Mid-pilot chats with tutoring families to adjust session times.

6
00:00:36.389 --> 00:00:44.756
Process: Looks at how delivery works in practice. For example: Checking whether tutors follow the session plan and pupils keep attending.

7
00:00:44.756 --> 00:00:52.011
Summative: Judges results at the end of a period. For example: End-of-year review: did pupils’ maths grades improve?

8
00:00:52.011 --> 00:01:04.170
Impact: Estimates the difference made compared with what would otherwise have happened; usually comes later. For example: Years on, comparing pupils with similar pupils who did not join.

9
00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:05.170
Why it matters

10
00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:10.844
1. It tells you whether to continue, change, scale up or stop.

11
00:01:10.844 --> 00:01:15.407
2. It finds unintended effects that monitoring can miss.

12
00:01:15.407 --> 00:01:22.081
3. It gives funders and partners a credible story of your contribution.

13
00:01:22.481 --> 00:01:23.081
What it guides

14
00:01:23.081 --> 00:01:27.644
1. Your end-of-pilot review, run by you at first.

15
00:01:27.644 --> 00:01:32.578
2. Your bigger decisions: register, grow, change course or stop.

16
00:01:32.578 --> 00:01:38.881
3. Your reports: findings, and how you responded to each one.

17
00:01:39.281 --> 00:01:39.881
What to avoid

18
00:01:39.881 --> 00:01:44.815
Covering all six criteria instead of your real questions.

19
00:01:44.815 --> 00:01:49.378
Promising rigorous impact evaluation you cannot yet afford.

20
00:01:49.378 --> 00:01:55.681
Finishing an evaluation with no plan to use its findings.

21
00:01:56.281 --> 00:01:58.081
You draft your evaluation plan for your pilot or first year.

22
00:01:58.081 --> 00:02:02.081
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:03.581 --> 00:02:06.681
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
